---
description: Rules for the SpaceCadetPinball libretro (MinUI / Miyoo Mini) project
alwaysApply: true
---
- NEVER add, generate, convert, or reference bytes of game assets (PINBALL.DAT, CADET.DAT, MIDI, sprites, sounds).
  Test fixtures must be synthetic. If a task appears to require an asset, stop and ask.
- The build MUST NOT read the DAT. The DAT is read only at runtime by the core from retro_game_info.path.
- New code: C++11 (compatible with upstream), header "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT", comments in English.
- Do not modify third_party/SpaceCadetPinball directly; changes go in patches/NNNN-*.patch with a rationale.
- No dynamic allocation, locks, I/O, or logs on the hot path of retro_run (except DEBUG-level log).
- Export only retro_* symbols (hidden visibility by default).
- Before opening a PR: run tools/check-no-proprietary.sh and unit/smoke tests.
- Items marked [VERIFICAR] in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md must be confirmed in code before implementing.
- Default controls follow the OnionOS Miyoo Mini port map (shoulders = flippers, A/B = plunger,
  D-pad = nudges / high scores, Start = pause, Select = new game). Do not reopen that map without
  an explicit decision recorded in docs/.
